  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> be the radius of the largest circle passing through the focus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/807de1a8-d722-452e-8c32-2df7ef662bcd-d48.png\" style=\"width: 325px; height: 250px;\" /></p><p>Clearly, centre of the circle will be on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>-axis and its coordinates are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>The equation of the circle, is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p><p>It touches <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math>. Therefore, the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> must have equal roots.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>Hence, option (b) is correct.</p>",
